        "original_id": "f781a47e-0cd9-5cc2-b681-66281080ceab",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Robey-Peters Gun-Carrier\n- Companies: Robey & Company Limited\n- Organizations: Royal Naval Air Service (RNAS)\n- Places: Bracebridge Heath, Lincoln, England\n- Topics: Population\n\nFacts:\n- The Robey-Peters Gun-Carrier was a British three-seater armed tractor biplane.\n- Robey & Company Limited designed and built the Robey-Peters Gun-Carrier at Bracebridge Heath, Lincoln.\n- The Royal Naval Air Service (RNAS) was the intended service for the Robey-Peters Gun-Carrier.\n- Bracebridge Heath is a commuter village about 2 miles south of Lincoln, England.\n- Bracebridge Heath had a population of 4,530 at the 2001 census.\n- Bracebridge Heath had a population of 5,656 at the 2011 census.",
